one of the requests I get more often  than any others in the comments section  of YouTube is to share some of my  favorite books some of the books I found  the most helpful in business in fitness  and working out in self-development  psychology and so that's what I'm gonna  do now for now I just want to share some  of my favorite business and productivity  that have helped me with my online  endeavors deep work by Cal Newport as  someone who regularly writes 15,000  words or more a day this book really  speaks to me it discusses the importance  of working for intense undisturbed  periods now to get the most from those  stints turns out you can get a heck of a  lot done when you aren't answering  emails all day or doing admin or dealing  with other communication overhead I wish  more businesses would read this book  because managers can learn a lot from it  by just letting their staff actually get  to work instead of pestering them all  the time probably my favorite concept in  here is the idea of productive  meditation this is meditation where the  objective isn't to completely empty your  mind but rather to dedicate some set  time to solving a problem or creative  challenge the personal MBA by Josh  Kaufman this book promises to be an MBA  in book form like the 4-hour workweek  that promises of course a little  hyperbolic what it is though is a  particularly comprehensive guide to  business that more than anything teaches  you to adopt the right mindset and to  see the bigger picture in business I  think the most important tip is to  understand your value proposition as per  the old saying you don't sell hats you  sell warm heads keys to understand the  emotional drive that your product or  service has how can you make your  customers lives better  how will they feel understanding this  will lead to far better branding and  marketing then there's the idea of  counterfactual simulation which is where  you run through possible futures in your  head and wonder whether or not you're  prepared for them in the book Josh  Callen talks about how this can help  with your business's resilience but I  also like to use this in my personal  life for instance if I'm going somewhere  and I'm not sure if I've remembered  everything I need to bring with me then  I simulate what's gonna happen in my  head and at each step ask if I've got  the thing that I need at that point in  the simulation thriving in the gig  economy freelancing online for tech  professionals and entrepreneurs by  adamson its key biased me surely not  this is of course my book and it's one  that unsurprisingly  I  also recommend it's a guide to working  online as a freelancer which is one of  the decisions that I made that  ultimately contributed most greatly to  my happiness  productivity health and lifestyle I  design this book to provide everything  you might need to know when starting out  your own business online one point I'm  particularly proud of though is the  description of the transhuman business  model a concept that I managed to sneak  into a technical book somehow the  general idea here is that you can scale  a one-man business by increasing your  own efficiency to superhuman degrees in  other words you don't have to increase  the rate you charge if you can increase  your output and being self-employed  means that the only limit on this is  your own capabilities new thinking by  dagoba I'll trade you can tell that I  like this book because my testimonial is  on the front cover I've worked with the  go-go aka cold fusion so I know  firsthand that he's a stand-up guy as  well as extremely interesting and  talented that's the side though this  book is a fascinating look at the impact  of various technologies throughout  history and as someone who loves the  impact that an individual mind or a  single idea can make on the future it's  just a great tour highlights include  quantum computing and the opening look  at Nikola Tesla the 4-hour workweek by  Tim Ferriss 